//ERR 13 3 13 13
//MSG="This function does not return a value in all control paths"

// Every path is covered except one: the outer `else` returns and the inner `if`
// returns, but taking the outer branch without the inner one runs off the end.
// `classify(5)` is that path.
//
// The uncovered path is buried, so this is what stops a shallow implementation
// that only looks at the last statement of the body, or that stops descending
// once it has seen a `ret` at some level.
//
// 27_nested_if_else_returns_on_every_leaf.cpl is the accepted form.

fn classify n
    if n > 0
        if n > 10
            ret 2
    else
        ret 0

fn main
    out "{classify(5)}"
